But I'm afraid the test subject won't be ready for transport until 1700 hours.

112
00:07:40,386 --> 00:07:41,686
We need it sooner.

113
00:07:42,306 --> 00:07:45,486
Do whatever it takes to have the subject ready by 1600 hours.

114
00:07:45,886 --> 00:07:49,026
If we screw this up, the human race is extinct.

115
00:07:49,406 --> 00:07:49,706
Sir!

116
00:07:53,286 --> 00:07:54,606
Hey, Kurato!

117
00:07:54,606 --> 00:08:01,166
Brother Seishiro, what are you doing here?

118
00:08:01,346 --> 00:08:03,266
Father wanted me to come by and say hello.

119
00:08:04,826 --> 00:08:07,006
So he wants you to keep tabs on me.

120
00:08:07,506 --> 00:08:09,266
I'm surprised he didn't send you earlier.

121
00:08:09,586 --> 00:08:12,366
If our intel's correct, the nobles are going to attack soon.

122
00:08:12,366 --> 00:08:16,226
You sure you're going to be able to handle that kind of fight by yourself?

123
00:08:16,906 --> 00:08:18,966
Father won't tolerate any screw-ups.

124
00:08:19,186 --> 00:08:20,806
They'll be hell to pay if you lose.

125
00:08:21,066 --> 00:08:22,786
Do you think I'm worried about him?

126
00:08:22,786 --> 00:08:26,546
Hey, take this seriously.

127
00:08:28,066 --> 00:08:30,886
Sorry, but you just sound so ridiculous.

128
00:08:31,746 --> 00:08:33,566
If I fail now, it's over.

129
00:08:33,906 --> 00:08:35,466
Our entire species is dead.

130
00:08:35,966 --> 00:08:38,346
And you still expect me to be afraid of the old man?

131
00:08:38,506 --> 00:08:40,066
Hey, you better watch what you're saying.

132
00:08:40,206 --> 00:08:43,026
If I report your attitude to Father, he might strip you of your...

133
00:08:43,026 --> 00:08:47,926
Cowards who are too scared to fight on the front lines should shut up and stay out of the way.

134
00:08:48,566 --> 00:08:51,166
A coward? You're going to regret that!

135
00:08:51,886 --> 00:08:55,866
Brother, did you just put your hands on me?

136
00:08:56,926 --> 00:08:59,266
Hey, I've got orders for Father to observe you.

137
00:08:59,746 --> 00:09:01,086
He won't let you hurt me.

138
00:09:01,186 --> 00:09:02,946
Father is very resourceful.

139
00:09:02,946 --> 00:09:05,846
But how could he protect you if you were to die right now?

140
00:09:05,846 --> 00:09:15,706
Kirito Hiragi, I'm arresting you for Les Majesté against our father.

141
00:09:16,346 --> 00:09:18,386
I order you to restrain this man!

142
00:09:25,886 --> 00:09:26,886
You're crazy!

143
00:09:27,046 --> 00:09:29,226
Do you honestly think you'll get away with this?

144
00:09:29,386 --> 00:09:30,366
Of course I will.

145
00:09:30,686 --> 00:09:33,766
Well, as long as I succeed at saving the world today.

146
00:09:35,846 --> 00:09:39,526
Lieutenant General, all of our squads will be ready to head out shortly.

147
00:09:40,026 --> 00:09:41,866
I'd recommend leaving in 30 minutes.

148
00:09:42,506 --> 00:09:42,926
Excellent.

149
00:09:43,406 --> 00:09:45,886
Wait, you're leaving? Where do you think you're going?

150
00:09:46,386 --> 00:09:48,386
The vampires are coming to attack us!

151
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:51,446
The vampires aren't going to step foot in Kanto.

152
00:09:51,746 --> 00:09:53,026
We're stopping them in Nagoya.

153
00:09:54,246 --> 00:09:55,246
You bastard!

154
00:09:55,626 --> 00:09:59,826
I dispatched the Shibuya troops because you said you could hold off our enemies in Shinjuku!

155
00:10:01,646 --> 00:10:05,786
Kirito, what have you been doing behind Father's back?

156
00:10:05,846 --> 00:10:11,506
Do you really think you could disobey the leader of the demon army and live?

157
00:10:11,686 --> 00:10:13,106
You can't be that stupid!

158
00:10:13,106 --> 00:10:27,026
You're lucky, Seishiro.

159
00:10:27,446 --> 00:10:31,146
You're a real pain in the ass, but you're always loyal to authority.

160
00:10:31,806 --> 00:10:33,726
You'll make a good servant later.

161
00:10:33,726 --> 00:10:43,166
But for the time being, you'll be locked up.

162
00:10:43,706 --> 00:10:45,046
I'll use you when I return.

163
00:10:45,046 --> 00:11:05,826
Hey, let me go already!

164
00:11:06,346 --> 00:11:08,386
Dammit, you can't just drag me around everywhere!

165
00:11:13,386 --> 00:11:15,886
I can't believe you guys.

166
00:11:16,846 --> 00:11:19,306
You're really just going to leave Gurren behind to die?

167
00:11:20,466 --> 00:11:21,626
Hey, Shinoa.

168
00:11:21,986 --> 00:11:22,546
Yes?

169
00:11:23,206 --> 00:11:24,386
He's your team member.

170
00:11:25,106 --> 00:11:26,846
It's your job to shut him up.

171
00:11:26,846 --> 00:11:29,966
You listen.

172
00:11:31,326 --> 00:11:34,666
If we all go back, we might be able to save him.

173
00:11:35,766 --> 00:11:36,666
I'm sorry.

174
00:11:36,666 --> 00:11:42,466
But we made a promise before the mission started.

175
00:11:43,026 --> 00:11:46,326
You agreed that when the time came to retreat, you'd leave no matter what.

176
00:11:46,886 --> 00:11:47,286
Yeah.

177
00:11:50,526 --> 00:11:51,826
But still...

178
00:11:51,826 --> 00:11:52,986
Look at the Major General.

179
00:11:53,386 --> 00:11:57,406
He's known the Lieutenant Colonel longer than you have, but he understands our duty.

180
00:11:58,006 --> 00:11:58,726
You see?

181
00:11:58,726 --> 00:12:04,666
So, we're just gonna...

182
00:12:04,666 --> 00:12:06,246
It's not that we're abandoning him.

183
00:12:07,806 --> 00:12:09,946
We're actually honoring his orders.

184
00:12:10,626 --> 00:12:13,826
Remember, the point of the mission wasn't to come back alive.

185
00:12:14,226 --> 00:12:15,226
The goal was...

186
00:12:15,226 --> 00:12:15,606
Victory.

187
00:12:16,146 --> 00:12:16,546
I know.

188
00:12:17,726 --> 00:12:19,446
We still have work to do.

189
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:21,166
And people to protect.

190
00:12:22,006 --> 00:12:24,706
If Gurren were here, he'd tell you to complete your mission.

191
00:12:25,866 --> 00:12:26,586
You're right.

192
00:12:26,586 --> 00:12:29,686
Major General Shinya.

193
00:12:31,186 --> 00:12:31,706
Goshi.

194
00:12:32,426 --> 00:12:34,106
Your quick thinking saved us back there.

195
00:12:34,866 --> 00:12:36,646
Is everybody else all right?

196
00:12:37,246 --> 00:12:37,586
Yeah.

197
00:12:38,126 --> 00:12:39,246
In a manner of speaking.

198
00:12:45,486 --> 00:12:47,006
There's no time for regret.

199
00:12:47,466 --> 00:12:48,366
We have to move.

200
00:12:48,966 --> 00:12:50,246
Tell us what your orders are.

201
00:12:53,486 --> 00:12:54,326
All right.

202
00:12:54,706 --> 00:12:56,026
Let's find Narumi's team.

203
00:12:56,586 --> 00:12:58,966
They should have saved all the hostages by now.

204
00:12:59,206 --> 00:13:02,206
It's likely that they'll be waiting for us at the rendezvous point.

205
00:13:02,946 --> 00:13:05,426
You want us to ditch Gurren and put the mission first.

206
00:13:06,146 --> 00:13:07,326
Like he doesn't matter.

207
00:13:08,166 --> 00:13:09,846
Like you don't care what happens to him.

208
00:13:12,886 --> 00:13:13,666
I care.

209
00:13:14,386 --> 00:13:15,586
We can't give up.

210
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:19,206
We're living in a messed up world.

211
00:13:19,686 --> 00:13:22,646
If we don't protect our family, then why bother living at all?

212
00:13:23,466 --> 00:13:26,586
Why try to save it if we're just going to abandon the people we care about?

213
00:13:30,586 --> 00:13:31,466
Gurren is...

214
00:13:31,466 --> 00:13:32,646
His family.

215
00:13:38,206 --> 00:13:39,346
He saved me.

216
00:13:39,346 --> 00:14:01,966
I heard you were screaming in your sleep again.

217
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:11,526
What kind of nightmare was it this time?

218
00:14:11,526 --> 00:14:15,126
The same as always.

219
00:14:15,366 --> 00:14:18,326
I had to watch a vampire kill everyone I cared about.

220
00:14:19,486 --> 00:14:21,886
And you wet the bed again, didn't you, kid?

221
00:14:22,886 --> 00:14:23,806
I'm not a baby.

222
00:14:23,866 --> 00:14:24,866
I've never wet the bed.

223
00:14:24,866 --> 00:14:27,486
It was just a dream.

224
00:14:28,106 --> 00:14:28,986
Go back to sleep.

225
00:14:29,366 --> 00:14:30,806
You're starting to be a real pain.

226
00:14:31,266 --> 00:14:32,026
What do you know?

227
00:14:33,986 --> 00:14:36,826
Why don't I hang out in here until you fall asleep again?

228
00:14:37,386 --> 00:14:38,406
Would you like that?

229
00:14:40,266 --> 00:14:41,166
Not really.

230
00:14:47,146 --> 00:14:47,946
Hey, Gurren.

231
00:14:48,546 --> 00:14:49,646
Shut up and go to sleep.

232
00:14:49,926 --> 00:14:50,786
I'm reading here.

233
00:14:51,566 --> 00:14:54,006
I've been trying to figure out why you saved me.

234
00:14:54,866 --> 00:14:56,366
I don't have a family anymore.

235
00:14:56,986 --> 00:14:58,466
I've never really had one.

236
00:14:59,186 --> 00:15:00,346
Not since I was born.

237
00:15:02,506 --> 00:15:04,386
My parents tried to kill me.

238
00:15:05,546 --> 00:15:08,466
And then when I finally found a new family, I lost them too.

239
00:15:09,846 --> 00:15:11,006
Maybe I'm cursed.

240
00:15:12,006 --> 00:15:13,466
I don't know why I'm alive.

241
00:15:14,406 --> 00:15:15,846
Or if I'm even worth it.

242
00:15:17,506 --> 00:15:19,406
Do you find life to be painful?

243
00:15:22,866 --> 00:15:23,826
I don't know.

244
00:15:24,866 --> 00:15:36,606
It hurts so much.

245
00:15:36,606 --> 00:15:38,426
It hurts so much, Gurren.

246
00:15:38,426 --> 00:15:46,126
Then you and I are the same.

247
00:15:51,066 --> 00:15:54,826
A long time ago, I couldn't save someone important to me.

248
00:15:54,826 --> 00:16:06,326
But I'm still here.

249
00:16:06,326 --> 00:16:08,226
You're still alive and miserable.

250
00:16:09,566 --> 00:16:10,346
That's life.

251
00:16:10,746 --> 00:16:12,426
It's full of things you can't escape.

252
00:16:13,046 --> 00:16:16,446
You have to eat, crap, sleep, remember when you'd rather forget.

253
00:16:17,446 --> 00:16:22,246
The thing is, one day you might be able to keep someone else from hurting the way you do.

254
00:16:22,246 --> 00:16:23,746
You can help them.

255
00:16:24,406 --> 00:16:27,206
So you just have to endure and wait for that day to come.

256
00:16:29,046 --> 00:16:29,946
Until then.

257
00:16:30,586 --> 00:16:35,606
Whenever life feels like it's too painful to go on, just concentrate on killing vampires.

258
00:16:35,606 --> 00:16:38,066
That'll help give you some focus, at least.

259
00:16:39,106 --> 00:16:39,826
Yeah, okay.

260
00:16:40,186 --> 00:16:41,646
I suppose I can do that.

261
00:16:43,606 --> 00:16:45,986
All you have to do is survive, you.

262
00:16:45,986 --> 00:16:50,646
Until that moment you find something that makes life worth living again.

263
00:16:55,206 --> 00:16:56,826
One day you'll feel better.

264
00:16:56,826 --> 00:16:59,326
I promise.

265
00:17:00,766 --> 00:17:03,826
